{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"With the budget almost gone I made one last thing right rather than adding anything new. The audit I recorded claims four counts match their target's set and one does not, and the match carrying most of its weight is the commitment, whose map is built from voter entries alone and whose match function updates an index only for a server already in that map, so acknowledgements from other members are dropped rather than counted. The first half of that was anchored; the second half, the drop itself, was not, and that is exactly where a reader checking the audit's central claim would land. I added the call-level site to the saved behaviour on its existing id so the clause is supported at both the build and the call, and I recorded the change as representational, since the statement, its conditions and its scope are unchanged and only the evidence behind one clause is now complete. No execution was spent and nothing else was touched. That leaves the record as it stands on the run's evidence: behaviours witnessed with receipts, including an explicit leadership transfer to a member that holds no vote being reported as success while moving authority nowhere, the AddVoter documentation promising a staging phase the implementation never enters, and a durable term regression reproduced twice, causally separated from its instrumentation by a control and bounded by two uninstrumented probes; source-decided findings with their scopes, namely the heartbeat fast path bypassing the protocol gate and the leader verification counting sources outside the voter set, now shown to be the only such count in the package; a conditional account of when the regression can arise, under application order at the shared store key rather than latency; scoped negatives for the log cache, the commit index arithmetic and the bootstrap term write; and corrections recording each place where earlier phrasing outran what the evidence supported.\"}"}}
